{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FOUR_TICKET_PROSE_AUDIT_FALLBACK:d6669496:unable\n\nThe unable-wingless-bustard MCP sequence was stopped after edit_ticket returned result=ok but push_status.state=pending (push-transport-failed: git timed out after 30s; unpushed=3). A terminal, idempotent MCP edit retry reconciled that backlog and returned push_status.state=ok with null warnings. The next MCP set_file_impact wrote nothing and failed after 181s because the live MCP server process (pid=1) held the tracker lock for 244s; a single follow-up MCP show_ticket then timed out at the client deadline after 300s.\n\nPer the documented fallback contingency, the remaining operations used the frozen audit worktree's repo-venv CLI, serialized: set-file-impact exited 0 and an immediate JSON readback matched all 18 ordered path/reason rows exactly; set-verify-commands exited 0 and an immediate normalized JSON readback matched all seven dd_id/dd_text/command rows exactly. No plan review, claim, source edit, implementation test/gate, transition, commit, or code push was performed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788638238791026001,"uuid":"097ff1cc-37ff-4f92-b67b-96876880d527"}